      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "As I reflect on my recent endeavors, I'm reminded of the cramped galley I found myself in. The air was thick with the salty residue of sea spray and the faint scent of cooking. I'd been exploring this space, taking in the simple details of its layout: a doorway leading north and a hatch in the floor that plunged down into darkness to the south.\n\nA kettle had caught my attention, lying abandoned on the floor. Without much thought, I picked it up, adding it to my small collection of belongings. My inventory wasn't extensive, but it was a start. I'd been trying to get a sense of what I had with me, so I'd made a mental note of the kettle.\n\nAs I held the kettle, I couldn't help but think about its story. Had it been used to make tea or boil water for some other purpose? The answers, much like the kettle's intended use, remained a mystery. Still, I'd decided to take a closer look at the kettle, examining its worn surface and wondering about its history.",
