    {
      "run": 5,
      "steps": 12,
      "narrative": "As I look around, I realize that I must have been a sailor on a ship, perhaps a cargo vessel or a fishing boat. I've been exploring the cramped galley, where I first found a kettle that was covered in salt. I took it with me, not sure why I needed it, but it's been with me ever since.\n\nI've been wandering through the ship, trying to make sense of my surroundings. I went north through the store, where I found a coil of rope that was also stiff with salt. I picked it up, but then dropped it, deciding it was more trouble than it was worth.\n\nAs I continued on my way, I climbed the stairs to a landing where I found a brass key and a window that doesn't open. The key doesn't seem to serve any purpose, but it's been a curiosity of mine ever since I found it. Now, I'm just trying to piece together how I got here and what my next move should be.",
